{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01ENeXmBRRc1FiorDcKBroRr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've now read the full paper and the review context. Let me also load the distilled writing skill for additional context, then dispatch two reviewers in parallel.\n\nLet me summarize what I've read:\n\n**Paper**: \"The Likert Blindspot: Detecting Hidden Style Bias in LLM Judges via Controlled Style Decomposition\"\n\n**Key contributions**:\n1. CSD pipeline: NLI-gated content control + per-axis style manipulation + position-controlled pairwise comparison + GEE decomposition\n2. Likert Blindspot: 9/10 BT-significant cells show Likert NS (90% blindspot rate)\n\n\n3. The confound structure varies by axis—verbosity acts as pure style, formality shows conditional effects, while register is dominated by originality factors\n4. Susceptibility differs across models, with verbosity affecting all three judges but formality only impacting two\n\nThe experiments span four different LLM judges across three benchmarks and three style dimensions, with multiple robustness checks including scaled replication, rewriter independence, placebo controls, and ablations of the NLI gating mechanism.\n\nNow I'm cross-referencing the imagined experiments against what's actually covered in the paper—checking which ones made it into the final tables and which ones are still pending.\n\nLooking through the list, all eleven experiments are accounted for across the various tables, so the paper has solid experimental coverage. Now I need to set up the review process by assigning the two reviewers to their respective domains and then coordinate the full roundtable discussion.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14400,"cache_read_input_tokens":38155,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14400},"outpu