{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01ENeXmBRRc1FiorDcKBroRr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Wj2CiaHKUBUwsCGmV3oRYB","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R1: Methods + Experiments review","prompt":"You are Reviewer 1 (R1) for an EMNLP 2026 ARR submission. Your focus: **Methods soundness and Experimental rigor**.\n\n## Venue Calibration (EMNLP 2026 ARR)\n- 5 = Award consideration (top 2.5%)\n- 4 = Conference-worthy (Main track, ~21% acceptance)\n- 3 = Findings-worthy\n- 2 = Major revision needed\n- 1 = Do not resubmit\nDimensions: Soundness (1-5), Excitement (1-5), Reproducibility (1-5)\n\n## Paper Summary\n**Title**: \"The Likert Blindspot: Detecting Hidden Style Bias in LLM Judges via Controlled Style Decomposition\"\n\nThe paper introduces Controlled Style Decomposition (CSD), a black-box diagnostic pipeline for detecting per-axis style bias in LLM judges. CSD combines:\n1. Per-axis style manipulation via LLM rewriter (Qwen3-32B default, GPT-4o alternative)\n2. NLI-gated content control (GPT-4o NLI model filters content-altered pairs)\n3. Position-controlled pairwise comparison (A/B swap) with Bradley-Terry preference + Likert scoring on identical stimuli\n4. GEE conditional decomposition: logit(P[prefer r'_a]) = β₀ + β_style·1[style shift] + β_orig·1[rewritten], yielding Style OR and Originality OR\n\n**Key findings**:\n- (C2a) Likert Blindspot: 9/10 BT-significant cells show Likert NS — 90% blindspot rate. Scaled replication (n=100→355) confirms d≈0 is structural, not power gap.\n- (C2b) Per-axis confound structure: verbosity = pure style (Style OR 5.48–13.10, Orig OR NS), formality = conditional (both ORs sig for GPT-4o/Qwen3), register = originality-dominated (Orig OR > Style OR)\n- (C1) CSD pipeline validated on 4 judges × 3 benchmarks × 3 axes\n- (C3) Architecture-dependent susceptibility: verbosity 3/3 target judges, formality 2/3\n\n**Experiments**:\n- 4 judges: GPT-4o, Qwen3-32B, Llama-3.3-70B, Claude Sonnet 4 (negative control)\n- 3 benchmarks: LLMBar (primary, 100 pairs), AlpacaEval, MT-Bench\n- 3 style axes: formality, verbosity, register\n- 12 tables covering: sensitivity comparison (Table 1), GEE decomposition (Table 2), GPT-4o verbosity/register (Table 3), formality across judges (Table 4), evidence matrix (Table 5), Llama-70B profile (Table 6), cross-benchmark formality (Table 7), scaled replication (Table 8), rewriter independence (Table 9), placebo control (Table 10), NLI ablation (Table 11), cross-axis gradient (Table 12)\n\n**Robustness controls (5-layer)**:\n1. Placebo control: original vs double-rewrite — rewriting artifact confirmed, GEE Orig OR models it\n2. NLI gate ablation: removing NLI gate *reverses* formality BT (41.7%), disconfirming amplification\n3. Cross-axis gradient: NLI rejection rate positively correlates with BT magnitude (3 data points, qualitative)\n4. Negative control: Claude Sonnet shows no significant bias on either axis\n5. Rewriter independence: GPT-4o rewriter produces statistically indistinguishable results from Qwen3 rewriter\n\n**Imagined experiment coverage**: The paper covers all 11 imagined experiments from the design document (multi-judge formality, multi-benchmark, Likert-vs-pairwise sensitivity, placebo control, scaled replication, non-Qwen rewriter, GPT-4o verbosity/register, Llama-70B third judge, NLI ablation, cross-axis gradient). Coverage is complete.\n\n## Your Task\nProduce a detailed review addressing:\n\n1. **Methodology Assessment**\n   - Is the CSD pipeline well-motivated and sound?\n   - Is the GEE model specification appropriate? Are there alternative specifications that should be considered (e.g., interaction terms, random effects)?\n   - Is the NLI gating approach a valid content control? What are its failure modes?\n   - Is the Bradley-Terry model appropriate for this setting?\n   - Position control (A/B swap) — is this sufficient?\n\n2. **Experimental Design**\n   - Sample sizes: LLMBar has 100 pairs — after NLI filtering, n≈86-88. Is this sufficient for the claims made?\n   - Statistical methodology: bootstrap BT (10K iterations), paired t-tests for Likert, robust sandwich SEs for GEE — appropriate?\n   - Multiple comparisons: the paper tests many judge×benchmark×axis cells. Is there correction for multiple testing?\n   - The \"90% blindspot rate\" denominator is only 10 cells. Is this a robust statistic?\n   - Scaled replication goes from n=100 to n=355 for one judge×axis only. Is broader replication needed?\n\n3. **Controls Assessment**\n   - Evaluate each of the 5 anti-amplification controls. Are they convincing?\n   - The cross-axis gradient has only 3 data points — is this meaningful evidence?\n   - Claude as negative control — is one negative control sufficient?\n   - Placebo control shows all judges prefer rewritten text — does this threaten the pure style claim for verbosity?\n\n4. **Reproducibility**\n   - Are the experimental details sufficient for reproduction?\n   - API-based judges (GPT-4o, Claude) may change over time\n   - Is the code/data availability mentioned?\n\n5. **Weaknesses**\n   - Identify the top 3-5 weaknesses in methods and experiments\n   - For each, assess severity (minor/moderate/major)\n\n6. **Missing Experiments or Analyses**\n   - What additional experiments would strengthen the paper?\n   - Any ablations that are missing?\n\nOutput format:\n```\n## R1: Methods and Experiments\n\n### Summary of Assessment\n[2-3 sentences]\n\n### Methodology\n[detailed assessment]\n\n### Experimental Design\n[detailed assessment]\n\n### Controls\n[detailed assessment]\n\n### Reproducibility\n[assessment]\n\n### Strengths (Methods/Experiments)\n1. ...\n2. ...\n3. ...\n\n### Weaknesses (Methods/Experiments)\n1. [severity] ...\n2. [severity] ...\n3. ...\n\n### Missing Experiments\n1. ...\n\n### Questions for Authors\n1. ...\n\n### Preliminary Scores\n- Soundness: X/5\n- Reproducibility: X/5\n- Overall lean: X.X (with brief justification calibrated to EMNLP 2026 acceptance rates)\n```\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14400,"cache_read_input_tokens":38155,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14400},"output_tokens":18,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"84c1e33b-a907-4d62-a6bc-d61bef62f953","uuid":"c53b09a5-a432-4149-8e06-0ec4a6c14654"}
