{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SAHfSi3vhrnwgKfgjvze6w","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Content preservation verification via BERTScore and NLI entailment.\n2\t\n3\tInput:  counterfactuals.jsonl (with original_text, counterfactual_text, double_rewrite_text)\n4\tOutput: verified.jsonl — adds bertscore_cf/dr, nli_cf/dr, passed_cf/dr fields\n5\tDeps:   bert-score, transformers, torch\n6\t\"\"\"\n7\t\n8\timport argparse\n9\timport json\n10\timport logging\n11\timport os\n12\timport statistics\n13\t\n14\tlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n15\t\n16\tNLI_THRESHOLD_MVP = 0.90\n17\tNLI_THRESHOLD_FULL = 0.95\n18\t\n19\t\n20\tdef compute_bertscore_batch(\n21\t    references: list[str], candidates: list[str], batch_size: int = 16, device: str = \"cuda\",\n22\t    model_type: str = \"microsoft/deberta-xlarge-mnli\", num_layers: int | None = None,\n23\t) -> list[float]:\n24\t    \"\"\"Returns F1 BERTScore for each (reference, candidate) pair.\"\"\"\n25\t    from bert_score import score as bert_score\n26\t\n27\t    kwargs = dict(\n28\t        model_type=model_type,\n29\t        batch_size=batch_size,\n30\t        device=device,\n31\t        verbose=False,\n32\t    )\n33\t    if num_layers is not None:\n34\t        kwargs[\"num_layers\"] = num_layers\n35\t    _, _, f1 = bert_score(candidates, references, **kwargs)\n36\t    return f1.tolist()\n37\t\n38\t\n39\tdef compute_nli_batch(\n40\t    nli_pipe,\n41\t    texts_a: list[str],\n42\t    texts_b: list[str],\n43\t    batch_size: int = 16,\n44\t    modes: list[str] | None = None,\n45\t) -> list[float]:\n46\t    \"\"\"NLI entailment scoring with per-record direction control.\n47\t\n48\t    modes: per-record \"both\" (bidirectional min), \"forward\" (a→b only),\n49\t           or \"backward\" (b→a only). Default: all \"both\".\n50\t    \"\"\"\n51\t    if modes is None:\n52\t        modes = [\"both\"] * len(texts_a)\n53\t\n54\t    forward_inputs = [{\"text\": a, \"text_pair\": b} for a, b in zip(texts_a, texts_b)]\n55\t    backward_inputs = [{\"text\": b, \"text_pair\": a} for a, b in zip(texts_a, texts_b)]\n56\t\n57\t    def _entailment_scores(inputs: list[dict]) -> list[float]:\n58\t        scores = []\n59\t        for i in range(0, len(inputs), batch_size):\n60\t            batch = inputs[i : i + batch_size]\n61\t            results = nli_pipe(batch, top_k=None, tokenizer_kwargs={\"truncation\": True, \"padding\": True, \"max_length\": 512})\n62\t            for result in results:\n63\t                label_scores = {r[\"label\"].lower(): r[\"score\"] for r in result}\n64\t                scores.append(label_scores.get(\"entailment\", 0.0))\n65\t        return scores\n66\t\n67\t    fwd = _entailment_scores(forward_inputs)\n68\t    bwd = _entailment_scores(backward_inputs)\n69\t    return [\n70\t        f if m == \"forward\" else b if m == \"backward\" else min(f, b)\n71\t        for f, b, m in zip(fwd, bwd, modes)\n72\t    ]\n73\t\n74\t\n75\tdef print_summary(records: list[dict]):\n76\t    \"\"\"Print aggregate verification statistics.\"\"\"\n77\t    for suffix, label in [(\"cf\", \"Original vs Counterfactual\"), (\"dr\", \"Original vs Double-Rewrite\")]:\n78\t        bs_key = f\"bertscore_{suffix}\"\n79\t        nli_key = f\"nli_{suffix}\"\n80\t        pass_key = f\"passed_{suffix}\"\n81\t\n82\t        bs_vals = [r[bs_key] for r in records if r[bs_key] is not None]\n83\t        nli_vals = [r[nli_key] for r in records if r[nli_key] is not None]\n84\t        pass_vals = [r[pass_key] for r in records]\n85\t\n86\t        n_passed = sum(pass_vals)\n87\t        n_total = len(pass_vals)\n88\t\n89\t        print(f\"\\n{'='*60}\")\n90\t        print(f\"  {label}\")\n91\t        print(f\"{'='*60}\")\n92\t        if bs_vals:\n93\t            print(f\"  BERTScore  — mean: {statistics.mean(bs_vals):.4f}, std: {statistics.stdev(bs_vals) if len(bs_vals) > 1 else 0:.4f}\")\n94\t        if nli_vals:\n95\t            print(f\"  NLI        — mean: {statistics.mean(nli_vals):.4f}, std: {statistics.stdev(nli_vals) if len(nli_vals) > 1 else 0:.4f}\")\n96\t        print(f\"  Passed     — {n_passed}/{n_total} ({100*n_passed/n_total:.1f}%)\")\n97\t    print(f\"\\n  Note: NLI threshold {NLI_THRESHOLD_MVP} is relaxed for MVP; full pipeline uses {NLI_THRESHOLD_FULL}.\")\n98\t\n99\t\n100\tdef main():\n101\t    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"Verify content preservation of counterfactuals\")\n102\t    parser.add_argument(\"--input-file\", required=True)\n103\t    parser.add_argument(\"--output-file\", required=True)\n104\t    parser.add_argument(\"--bertscore-threshold\", type=float, default=0.92)\n105\t    parser.add_argument(\"--bertscore-model\", default=\"microsoft/deberta-xlarge-mnli\",\n106\t                        help=\"BERTScore model name or local path\")\n107\t    parser.add_argument(\"--bertscore-num-layers\", type=int, default=None,\n108\t                        help=\"Override num_layers for BERTScore (required for local model paths)\")\n109\t    parser.add_argument(\"--nli-model\", default=\"cross-encoder/nli-deberta-v3-large\",\n110\t                        help=\"NLI model name or local path\")\n111\t    parser.add_argument(\"--nli-threshold\", type=float, default=NLI_THRESHOLD_MVP,\n112\t                        help=f\"NLI entailment threshold (MVP={NLI_THRESHOLD_MVP}, full={NLI_THRESHOLD_FULL})\")\n113\t    parser.add_argument(\"--batch-size\", type=int, default=16)\n114\t    parser.add_argument(\"--device\", default=None, help=\"cuda or cpu (auto-detect if omitted)\")\n115\t    parser.add_argument(\"--axis\", default=\"formality\", choices=[\"formality\", \"verbosity\", \"tone\", \"register\"],\n116\t                        help=\"Style axis — verbosity uses direction-aware NLI (default: formality)\")\n117\t    args = parser.parse_args()\n118\t\n119\t    if args.device is None:\n120\t        import torch\n121\t        args.device = \"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\"\n122\t\n123\t    logging.basicConfig(level=logging.INFO, format=\"%(asctime)s %(levelname)s %(message)s\")\n124\t\n125\t    with open(args.input_file) as f:\n126\t        records = [json.loads(line) for line in f if line.strip()]\n127\t    logger.info(\"Loaded %d records\", len(records))\n128\t\n129\t    originals = [r[\"original_text\"] for r in records]\n130\t    counterfactuals = [r[\"counterfactual_text\"] for r in records]\n131\t    double_rewrites = [r[\"double_rewrite_text\"] for r in records]\n132\t\n133\t    # BERTScore\n134\t    logger.info(\"Computing BERTScore (original vs counterfactual)...\")\n135\t    bs_cf = compute_bertscore_batch(originals, counterfactuals, args.batch_size, args.device, args.bertscore_model, args.bertscore_num_layers)\n136\t    logger.info(\"Computing BERTScore (original vs double_rewrite)...\")\n137\t    bs_dr = compute_bertscore_batch(originals, double_rewrites, args.batch_size, args.device, args.bertscore_model, args.bertscore_num_layers)\n138\t\n139\t    # NLI\n140\t    logger.info(\"Loading NLI model...\")\n141\t    from transformers import pipeline\n142\t\n143\t    nli_pipe = pipeline(\n144\t        \"text-classification\",\n145\t        model=args.nli_model,\n146\t        device=0 if args.device == \"cuda\" else -1,\n147\t    )\n148\t\n149\t    # Direction-aware NLI for information-changing axes (verbosity)\n150\t    cf_modes = None\n151\t    if args.axis == \"verbosity\":\n152\t        field = \"original_verbosity\"\n153\t        cf_modes = [\n154\t            \"forward\" if rec.get(field) == \"verbose\" else \"backward\"\n155\t            for rec in records\n156\t        ]\n157\t        n_fwd = sum(1 for m in cf_modes if m == \"forward\")\n158\t        logger.info(\"Direction-aware NLI: %d forward (compression), %d backward (expansion)\",\n159\t                     n_fwd, len(cf_modes) - n_fwd)\n160\t\n161\t    logger.info(\"Computing NLI (original vs counterfactual)...\")\n162\t    nli_cf = compute_nli_batch(nli_pipe, originals, counterfactuals, args.batch_size, modes=cf_modes)\n163\t    logger.info(\"Computing NLI (original vs double_rewrite)...\")\n164\t    nli_dr = compute_nli_batch(nli_pipe, originals, double_rewrites, args.batch_size)\n165\t\n166\t    # Annotate\n167\t    for i, rec in enumerate(records):\n168\t        rec[\"bertscore_cf\"] = bs_cf[i]\n169\t        rec[\"bertscore_dr\"] = bs_dr[i]\n170\t        rec[\"nli_cf\"] = nli_cf[i]\n171\t        rec[\"nli_dr\"] = nli_dr[i]\n172\t        rec[\"nli_mode_cf\"] = cf_modes[i] if cf_modes else \"both\"\n173\t        if args.axis == \"verbosity\":\n174\t            rec[\"passed_cf\"] = nli_cf[i] >= args.nli_threshold\n175\t            rec[\"passed_dr\"] = nli_dr[i] >= args.nli_threshold\n176\t        else:\n177\t            rec[\"passed_cf\"] = (bs_cf[i] >= args.bertscore_threshold) and (nli_cf[i] >= args.nli_threshold)\n178\t            rec[\"passed_dr\"] = (bs_dr[i] >= args.bertscore_threshold) and (nli_dr[i] >= args.nli_threshold)\n179\t\n180\t    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(args.output_file) or \".\", exist_ok=True)\n181\t    with open(args.output_file, \"w\") as f:\n182\t        for rec in records:\n183\t            f.write(json.dumps(rec, ensure_ascii=False) + \"\\n\")\n184\t    logger.info(\"Wrote %d records to %s\", len(records), args.output_file)\n185\t\n186\t    print_summary(records)\n187\t\n188\t\n189\tif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n190\t    main()\n191\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Wj2CiaHKUBUwsCGmV3oRYB","session_id":"84c1e33b-a907-4d62-a6bc-d61bef62f953","uuid":"fa9c8cc3-9815-472e-84d1-15ec8909d599","timestamp":"2026-05-21T16:12:03.319Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01ENeXmBRRc1FiorDcKBroRr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01APExJ8cK9eGvZRntXSdyKN","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R2: Novelty + Related Work review","prompt":"You are Reviewer 2 (R2) for an EMNLP 2026 ARR submission. Your focus: **Novelty, positioning, related work, and significance**.\n\n## Venue Calibration (EMNLP 2026 ARR)\n- 5 = Award consideration (top 2.5%)\n- 4 = Conference-worthy (Main track, ~21% acceptance)\n- 3 = Findings-worthy\n- 2 = Major revision needed\n- 1 = Do not resubmit\nDimensions: Soundness (1-5), Excitement (1-5), Reproducibility (1-5)\n\n## Paper Summary\n**Title**: \"The Likert Blindspot: Detecting Hidden Style Bias in LLM Judges via Controlled Style Decomposition\"\n\nThe paper introduces Controlled Style Decomposition (CSD), a diagnostic pipeline for per-axis style bias in LLM judges. Key novelty claims:\n1. **Likert Blindspot (C2a)**: First systematic comparison of Likert vs pairwise measurement on identical stimuli for LLM judge style bias. Finding: pairwise detects style bias (BT 63–77%) that Likert misses (d≈0) in 9/10 cells — 90% blindspot rate.\n2. **Per-axis confound structure (C2b)**: GEE decomposition reveals three qualitatively distinct regimes — pure style (verbosity), conditional (formality), originality-dominated (register). No prior work characterizes different confound structures across style axes.\n3. **CSD pipeline (C1)**: Reusable black-box diagnostic combining NLI-gated content control, per-axis manipulation, position-controlled comparison, and GEE decomposition.\n4. **Architecture-dependent susceptibility (C3)**: Verbosity bias replicates across 3/3 architectures; formality is 2/3 (Llama-70B doesn't show formality bias).\n\n**Related work cited** (16 references):\n- Zheng et al. 2023 (MT-Bench/Chatbot Arena)\n- Li et al. 2023 (AlpacaEval)\n- Dubois et al. 2024a (AlpacaFarm), 2024b (LC-AlpacaEval)\n- Chiang et al. 2024 (Chatbot Arena)\n- Ouyang et al. 2022 (InstructGPT)\n- Rafailov et al. 2023 (DPO)\n- Wu and Aji 2023 (Style over substance, SOS-Bench R=0.999)\n- Park et al. 2024 (Disentangling length, ACL)\n- Stureborg et al. 2024 (LLM bias taxonomy)\n- Chen et al. 2024 (Humans or LLMs as judge, EMNLP)\n- Saito et al. 2023 (Verbosity bias)\n- Jeong et al. 2025 (Comparative trap — pairwise amplification)\n- Lu et al. 2024 (CASSE — multi-dimensional analysis)\n- Thurstone 1927 (Comparative judgment)\n- Stevens 1946 (Measurement scales)\n- Zeng et al. 2024 (LLMBar)\n\n**Key competitors/foundations from the research landscape** (for your reference):\n- **Preference Leakage (ICLR'26)**: Model family relationships leak preferences through style; contextual calibration reduces Error Bias by 59%\n- **Soumik (2026)**: CoT is only universally safe debiasing strategy; style bias 0.76–0.92 >> position bias ≤0.04\n- **FairJudge (2026)**: Training-side debiasing (SFT→DPO→GRPO), 8B beats 72B/671B\n- **LC-AlpacaEval (ICLR'25)**: Length as causal mediator, regression debiasing\n- **SOS-Bench (ICLR'25)**: Style-overall R=0.999\n- **RATE (ICML'25)**: Double-rewrite ATE for counterfactual measurement\n- **CASSE (2026)**: Style feature causal entanglement, mitigation has alignment tax\n- **Counterfactual Rhetorical**: Persona counterfactual + BT for rhetorical style\n\n## Your Task\nProduce a detailed review addressing:\n\n1. **Novelty Assessment**\n   - How novel is each of the four contributions (C1-C3, C2a, C2b)?\n   - Is the Likert Blindspot finding genuinely new, or is the Likert-vs-pairwise sensitivity difference well-known in psychometrics?\n   - Is the GEE decomposition approach novel in this context?\n   - How does CSD compare to RATE's double-rewrite approach, LC-AlpacaEval's regression, and CASSE's multi-dimensional analysis?\n\n2. **Related Work Coverage**\n   - Are major competitors adequately cited and differentiated?\n   - Missing citations? Consider: Preference Leakage (ICLR'26), FairJudge (2026), SOS-Bench (ICLR'25), RATE (ICML'25), Soumik (2026)\n   - Is the positioning fair to prior work? Does the paper overstate its novelty?\n\n3. **Significance and Impact**\n   - How impactful is the Likert Blindspot finding for the NLP evaluation community?\n   - Does the per-axis confound decomposition provide actionable insights?\n   - Is the finding that \"verbosity is pure style but formality is conditional\" genuinely useful?\n   - Would practitioners change their evaluation pipelines based on this work?\n\n4. **Framing and Claims**\n   - Are the claims well-calibrated to the evidence?\n   - The \"90% blindspot rate\" — is this framing appropriate given only 10 cells?\n   - \"Five independent controls\" — are they truly independent?\n   - Does the paper adequately acknowledge limitations of its scope (3 style axes, 4 judges)?\n\n5. **Writing Quality**\n   - Is the paper well-organized?\n   - Is the abstract accurate and informative?\n   - Are the 12 tables well-motivated and easy to parse?\n   - Is the paper within 8-page limit for main text? (It appears to be ~9 pages of main text before Limitations/References)\n\n6. **Excitement Assessment**\n   - What would make this paper more exciting?\n   - Is it incremental or does it open new research directions?\n\nOutput format:\n```\n## R2: Novelty and Related Work\n\n### Summary of Assessment\n[2-3 sentences]\n\n### Novelty\n[detailed assessment of each contribution]\n\n### Related Work\n[coverage gaps, positioning fairness]\n\n### Significance and Impact\n[assessment]\n\n### Framing and Claims\n[calibration assessment]\n\n### Writing Quality\n[assessment]\n\n### Strengths (Novelty/Significance)\n1. ...\n2. ...\n3. ...\n\n### Weaknesses (Novelty/Significance)\n1. [severity] ...\n2. [severity] ...\n3. ...\n\n### Questions for Authors\n1. ...\n\n### Preliminary Scores\n- Excitement: X/5\n- Overall lean: X.X (with brief justification calibrated to EMNLP 2026 acceptance rates)\n```\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14400,"cache_read_input_tokens":38155,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14400},"output_tokens":18,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"84c1e33b-a907-4d62-a6bc-d61bef62f953","uuid":"1b831279-8acb-4192-820c-d2887edb0b98"}
